---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Seek Privacy Policy"
  description="How Seek and the Seek website handle app data, website requests, and support emails."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <main class="page-main" id="content" tabindex="-1">
    <article class="prose section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>
        Privacy,
        <br />
        <span>in plain English.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="article-intro">
        Seek is designed to work locally without an account, analytics pipeline,
        or cloud service. This policy also explains the limited data involved
        when you visit this website or contact support.
      </p>
      <p class="policy-updated">
        Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-08">October 8, 2026</time>
      </p>

      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          Seek is developed by Venturian Ecom in the Netherlands. Contact
          details and business registration information are available on the{" "}
          <a href="https://venturiane.com/en/company-details/">
            Venturian Ecom company details page
          </a>
          .
        </p>

        <h2>Data handled by the Seek app</h2>
        <p>
          Seek processes search queries, preferences, favorites, and enabled
          local features on your Mac. Seek does not require an account and does
          not send this app data to a Seek server.
        </p>
        <p>
          Clipboard history is optional and off by default. When enabled,
          supported password-manager content and identified password fields are
          excluded from capture. You remain responsible for deciding whether
          clipboard history is appropriate for your Mac.
        </p>

        <h2>Website data</h2>
        <p>
          This website does not use advertising cookies or product analytics.
          Like most websites, its hosting and security providers may temporarily
          process technical request data such as an IP address, browser
          information, requested URL, and timestamp to deliver the site, prevent
          abuse, and diagnose failures.
        </p>

        <h2>Support emails</h2>
        <p>
          If you contact support, Venturian Ecom receives the information you
          choose to include, along with normal email metadata. It is used to
          answer your request and maintain relevant support records. Do not
          include passwords, private clipboard contents, or unrelated sensitive
          data.
        </p>

        <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
        <p>
          Venturian Ecom does not sell personal data. Data may be processed by
          infrastructure and email providers only where needed to operate the
          website or answer support requests, or when required by law. Support
          correspondence is retained only as long as reasonably needed for
          support, security, and legal obligations.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can disable optional local features inside Seek and remove the app
          from your Mac. For questions about personal data, access, correction,
          or deletion requests, email <!--email_off-->
          <a href="mailto:hello@venturiane.com?subject=Seek%20privacy">
            hello@venturiane.com
          </a>
          <!--/email_off-->.
        </p>

        <h2>Policy changes</h2>
        <p>
          Material changes will be published on this page with an updated date.
          Changes to app privacy behavior will also be called out in the
          relevant release notes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
